      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this would be ok. It basically allows cached_voltage to be returned by charget_get_voltage() whatever charger_set_voltage() does. Now what I don\u0027t understand/remember is how/why we weren\u0027t doing the 0 check before. The only thing I can conclude is that a write of 0 doesn\u0027t stick and reading it back is the lowest possible value.\n\nThis code appears to be wanting to set a minimum voltage that is higher than the minimum enforced by hardware. Is that true?",
