      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, my fuzzy recollection is that the charging state machine thinks 0 is valid and wants it to be returned from get(). If someone has this hardware, what is the value read back after writing 0. That would give us a more complete picture.\n\nAccording to the datasheet it says \"Any value below 4.096V results in 4.096V\". So I think we could step down all the way to 4.096V then level out and only when voltage is equal to 0 would be apply CHARGER_NVDC_VOLTAGE.",
